# "{7}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Destroy target permanent." On turn 3 Bot1 taps the Boulder for its mana (paying its {1} with a Mountain): with six other mana sources and
# the Boulder's mana in the pool, Bot1 holds seven mana, yet the destroy ability is refused because its {T} cost cannot be paid (CR 602.2). On turn 5, with the
# Boulder untapped and seven mana paid, the same ability is the positive control: it sacrifices the Boulder as a cost and destroys Bot2's Island, a land - "target permanent",
# not "nonland permanent". The seven mana was exactly seven (Mox Ruby, the eighth source, is untouched).

